      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for this. it's a decent start but it feels a bit thin. the software is actually flagging this version because the scientific name count is pretty low compared to what's usually expected for a \"high quality\" report. \n\ncould you expand on this? try to be more specific about the actual species observed in those groups (canopy dwellers, riverbank predators, avian, primates, etc). i really need the summary to be robust and detailed, but i am stressing—please don't just dump a list of names. it has to be a professional narrative that describes the health of the ecosystem. if it's just a list, the client will reject it immediately.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
